Z||000002||theogre||10-26-2001||07:53 PM||||I don't know allot about that company. They are one of the larger AC/Heating suppliers out there.<P>The most important thing in any AC compressor replacement is that the ACC/Dryer and the orifice tube also be replaced.<P>You might also consider installing a screen into the suction port. these protect the new compressor from crap left in the system by the dead one. These screens are made by<A HREF="http://www.airsept.com/" TARGET=_blank>AirSept</A>. I'm not sure where you can get them installed short of getting the whole kit.<P>AirSept also makes the blower controller used by some of the car makers. This controller run the blower to dry out the AC system to help keep it from stinking. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
